              "text": "the supreme lord of the city of Kāśī."
            }
          ]
        ],
        "bhavartha": "Kālabhairava holds a trident, a hatchet, a noose and a rod, and He is the first cause. His body is dark; He is the first god, imperishable and free from sickness. His might is terrible, He is the Lord, and He loves the wondrous tāṇḍava dance. The singer worships Him: Kālabhairava, the supreme lord of the city of Kāśī."
      },
      "hi": {
        "lines": [
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w1"
              ],
              "text": "जिनके हाथों में शूल, टङ्क (कुल्हाड़ी), पाश और दण्ड हैं,"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w1"
              ],
              "text": "जो आदि कारण हैं,"
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "refs": [
                "w2"
              ],
              "text": "जिनका शरीर श्याम है, जो आदिदेव और अविनाशी हैं,"
            },
            {
              "refs": [
                "w3"
              ],
              "text": "जिन्हें कोई रोग छू नहीं सकता,"
            }
          ],
          [
